course: dictionary
lesson: 5969
title: Maturity in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Maturity is a noun, and it has three main meanings. Most of the time you will meet the first two: being grown-up and sensible in how you think and behave, or being fully grown and developed. The third meaning is about money.
explain: «Some academies now group young players by maturity rather than only age.» Here maturity means how developed and grown-up a player is, not how many years old they are. Age counts the years you have lived. Maturity measures how far you have grown and developed.
explain: In school and PSHE, you «show maturity» when you act responsibly and stay calm, such as keeping your cool after losing a game. In science, an animal «reaches maturity» when it is fully grown and can have young. Always check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Maturity means being grown-up and sensible, being fully grown, or the date a loan or savings bond must be paid back.
fact: «Maturity» can describe animals, plants and fruit when they are fully grown or developed.
fact: «Show maturity» means to act responsibly and calmly, even when things are hard.
fact: Age is how many years old you are; maturity is how grown-up you are in how you think, behave and develop.
fact: Maturity is an uncountable noun, so we say «emotional maturity», not «a maturity».
exercise: «Some academies now group young players by maturity rather than only age.» Here maturity means | *How developed and grown-up a player is | The day the team must pay back a loan | The number of years a player has lived | The colour of the team kit
exercise: Ayesha stayed calm and sensible when the match went wrong. What does this show? | *Maturity | Barely | Hunger | Ancientness
exercise: In science, when does an animal reach maturity? | *When it is fully grown and can have young | When it is first born | When it has run out of food | When it has been painted
test: Which phrase means acting responsibly and calmly? | show a map | *show maturity | show your teeth | show off
test: A loan must be paid back by a set date. What is that date called in money terms? | The luminous date | The curt date | The famished date | *The maturity date
exam: Which sentence uses maturity to mean being fully grown? | The apple was treacherous to hold | *The apple had reached maturity and was ready to pick | The apple was painted bright red | The apple was sour and bruised
